=======================================================
 TERRAFORM STATE LOCKING - STUDY NOTES
=======================================================

WHAT IS STATE LOCKING?
-----------------------------------------------------
A safety mechanism that prevents two people (or two
CI jobs) from running "terraform apply" against the
SAME state file at the SAME time. Without it,
concurrent writes can corrupt terraform.tfstate.

When you run plan/apply, Terraform:
  1. Acquires a lock
  2. Reads/writes state
  3. Releases the lock

If someone else already holds the lock, your run will
fail/wait instead of racing to write state.


HOW LOCKING WORKS (DYNAMODB METHOD - CLASSIC)
-----------------------------------------------------
A separate DynamoDB table stores lock records, keyed
by "LockID". Terraform writes a lock item there before
touching the S3 state file, and deletes it when done.

# backend.tf
terraform {
  backend "s3" {
    bucket         = "my-company-tfstate-bucket"
    key            = "envs/prod/network/terraform.tfstate"
    region         = "us-east-1"
    dynamodb_table = "terraform-locks"
    encrypt        = true
  }
}

# DynamoDB table required for locking
resource "aws_dynamodb_table" "locks" {
  name         = "terraform-locks"
  billing_mode = "PAY_PER_REQUEST"
  hash_key     = "LockID"

  attribute {
    name = "LockID"
    type = "S"
  }
}


HOW LOCKING WORKS (NATIVE S3 LOCKFILE - TF 1.10+)
-----------------------------------------------------
Newer Terraform versions can lock natively using a
lockfile object in S3 itself -- no DynamoDB table
needed.

terraform {
  backend "s3" {
    bucket       = "my-company-tfstate-bucket"
    key          = "envs/prod/network/terraform.tfstate"
    region       = "us-east-1"
    encrypt      = true
    use_lockfile = true
  }
}


WHAT A LOCK ERROR LOOKS LIKE
-----------------------------------------------------
Error: Error acquiring the state lock

Lock Info:
  ID:        e5f6a1b2-....
  Path:      envs/prod/network/terraform.tfstate
  Operation: OperationTypeApply
  Who:       user@hostname
  Created:   2026-09-04 10:15:00 UTC


FIXING A STUCK LOCK
-----------------------------------------------------
Happens when a process crashes/gets killed mid-apply
and never releases the lock.

# Force-remove a stuck lock (use the Lock ID from the
# error message above)
terraform force-unlock <LOCK_ID>

CAUTION: only force-unlock if you're SURE no other
apply is actually running. Removing a lock during a
real in-progress apply can corrupt state.


KEY GOTCHAS
-----------------------------------------------------
  - Locking protects the STATE FILE, not your actual
    infra -- it won't stop two people writing
    conflicting .tf CODE, only conflicting state WRITES
  - DynamoDB table needs "LockID" as its hash key --
    exact name matters
  - Native S3 locking (use_lockfile) removes the need
    for a DynamoDB table, but requires Terraform 1.10+
  - Always double check before force-unlock -- it's a
    manual override, not a normal operation

